### 3.3 Malleability proof

Node/OpenSSL *accepts* the high-S variant of a valid signature; the verifier rejects it, proving the low-S rule is a deliberate cryptographic policy rather than a DER-parsing artifact:

```text
parsed r,s from Node DER signature
s is high-S: true
Node/OpenSSL crypto.verify accepts high-S DER: true
our verifyES256 rejects high-S: high-S signature rejected (ECDSA malleability)
```

